From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PrismML <noreply@prismml.ai>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:18:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Prism: HERMES_PRISM_CUT_RECOVERY=1 (a tool call cut by
 the output limit is not resent blind)

Stock Hermes, when a reply's tool call is cut by the output limit
(finish_reason "length"), resends the identical request up to 4 times without
telling the model, then ends the run with "Response truncated due to output
length limit". A model that tries to write a whole game in one write_file call
is usually cut again at the same point.

With HERMES_PRISM_CUT_RECOVERY=1, a cut tool call (not a network stub stall):
- is not executed; the cut assistant turn is kept with its visible text only (no
  partial tool call) and carries its own reasoning under "prism_cut_reasoning"
  (Bonsai-demo's logproxy.py turns that into reasoning_content when reasoning is
  kept across turns, and drops it otherwise);
- is followed by one user note naming the tool, its target path and the output
  tokens used, asking for the work in tool calls under ~8K tokens each;
- the loop continues with a new API call.
The same applies when a router rewrites finish_reason to "tool_calls" but the
arguments are truncated JSON: the stream builder does not "repair" truncated
arguments into an executable call, and the invalid-JSON path gets the same note
instead of the immediate stop. At most HERMES_PRISM_CR_MAX (4) recoveries per
segment (the counter resets after a tool call executes); after that the stock end
behaviour runs. Events go to HERMES_PRISM_CUT_RECOVERY_LOG (JSONL). Unset = stock.
